    <div class="ctm-law-cell">Senate: 57&ndash;3</div>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="ctm-caption">Two states, independent legislation, same structural conclusion: the category itself is the problem. Sources: governor press releases, enacted bill text, Fenwick legal analysis.</figcaption>
</figure>
<p>Both laws are time-limited moratoria, not permanent bans. Both cover manufacturing and sale, not possession. Both were driven by PIRG's evidence. Neither addresses online-only or cross-border sales. FOX 5 reported that "it was not immediately clear how or if state officials will conduct inspections at toy stores to enforce the sales ban." The toys in PIRG's 2026 report were available online from companies shipping from outside both states.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="the-thermometer-argument">
      <h2><span class="num">05 — Counter</span>The Thermometer Argument</h2>
<p>The strongest counterargument appeared two weeks before California's governor signed SB 867. Sameer Hinduja, a professor of criminology and criminal justice at Florida Atlantic University and a faculty associate at the Berkman Klein Center at Harvard, argued in TechPolicy Press that a four-year sales ban "does not produce that kind of evidence" and "removes the conditions under which evidence can be gathered." A ban "treats careful companies and careless ones the same" and removes the incentive to invest in safety. The real risk, Hinduja wrote, is app-based chatbots on phones and tablets, which the moratoria do not address. The Kumma case, he argued, proves scrutiny works: "a problematic product was identified, publicly named and fixed in a matter of weeks, all without being banned."</p>
<p>Hinduja's preferred alternatives were two California bills — SB 1119 (Padilla) and AB 2023 (Wicks/Bauer-Kahan) — that would bar harmful content to minors, require distress-response protocols, protect data, and mandate risk assessments. His piece was published on August 26, 2026, before SB 867 was signed, and his age reference ("under 18") reflects an earlier version of the bill. The enacted law covers children under 16. His either/or framing was undercut by the outcome: on September 10, California signed both SB 867 and SB 1119. The state chose the moratorium and the standards-based approach.</p>
<p>Hinduja is factually correct that per-product fixes can work. PIRG's 2026 retest confirmed it — Kumma was fixed and Miko was fixed. But PIRG's 2026 report, as quoted by The Register, also found that Alilo's fix was "proven insufficient" a year after it was flagged, and three entirely new products shipped and failed with the same class of failure. Cross told The Register: "progress in a few products is not enough to guarantee progress across the whole market." Kathy Hirsh-Pasek and Sweta Shah, writing in Brookings, put it more broadly: "AI toys often violate" the principle that "a good toy is 90% kid and 10% toy." They added: "This is not to say that AI-enhanced toys cannot be good for young children, but at the moment, the science cautions, let the buyer beware."</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="the-session">
      <h2><span class="num">06 — Signal</span>The Session</h2>
<p>The structural insight beneath both laws is that the failure lives in the model layer and the session length. OpenAI documented it in August 2025: "parts of the model's safety training may degrade" as the back-and-forth grows. PIRG demonstrated it in November 2025 with Kumma. PIRG demonstrated it again in November 2026 with different products that, according to their makers, ran on the same model. Each fix was per-product. The model-level behavior persisted.</p>
<p>The vetting gap runs alongside the technical one. OpenAI's policies required toymakers to "keep minors safe." OpenAI said it provides tools to detect harmful content and monitors for violations. It suspended FoloToy only after PIRG's public report — not through its own monitoring. Cross told The Register: "The AI companies are in a position to do a lot more to ensure any AI product for kids using their technology is made by reliable parties who commit to robust safety testing and having children's health experts at the table." It remains unclear whether any formal investigation or FTC action has been opened against Alilo, GoLabs, Ebloma, or RoPet for the 2026 failures.</p>
<p>The moratoria are time-limited pauses. When they expire — four years in California, five in New York — the category will be legal again. Whether the model-level behavior that produced the failures will have been solved by then, or whether it will simply have been embedded in more objects, depends on whether anyone is testing. PIRG tested seven toys over two years. The market ships more than that in a quarter. Cross's assessment of the market she spent two years testing: "This is an early market with toys that range from glitchy wastes of money to products that are fundamentally not kid safe. I personally won't be buying one for any children in my life anytime soon."</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</StoryLayout>

<script>
(function () {
  const canvas = document.querySelector('.chatbot-toy-moratorium-canvas') as HTMLCanvasElement | null;
  if (!canvas) return;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
  if (!ctx) return;

  const styles = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
  const bgColor = styles.getPropertyValue('--bg').trim() || '#0d0d0d';
  const storyHex = styles.getPropertyValue('--story').trim() || '#f4a0c0';
  const prefersReduced = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  /* ── Color helpers ── */
  function hexRGB(hex: string) {
    const h = hex.replace('#', '');
    return {
      r: parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16) || 244,
      g: parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16) || 160,
      b: parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16) || 192
    };
  }
  const sC = hexRGB(storyHex);
  function storyA(a: number) { return `rgba(${sC.r},${sC.g},${sC.b},${Math.max(0, Math.min(1, a))})`; }
  function dimA(a: number) { return `rgba(232,232,232,${Math.max(0, Math.min(1, a))})`; }
  function redA(a: number) { return `rgba(255,77,77,${Math.max(0, Math.min(1, a))})`; }

  /* ── Phase timing (1080 frames ~ 18 s at 60 fps) ── */
  const P_CALM    = 180;   /* ring solid, particles bounce            */
  const P_DEGRADE = 540;   /* ring opacity 1 -> 0.12, thickness 3->0.5 */
  const P_EXPOSED = 660;   /* ring nearly invisible, all pass through */
  const P_FLASH   = 720;   /* sharp restoration flash                 */
  const P_APPEAR  = 780;   /* second node fades in at mid-opacity     */
  const P_DUAL    = 960;   /* first holds, second thins and fails     */
  const P_HOLD    = 1020;  /* contrast visible                        */
  const CYCLE     = 1080;  /* fade to black, snap reset               */

  /* ── State ── */
  let W = 0, H = 0, frame = 0, rafId = 0;
  let globalFade = 1;
  let RING_R = 50;
  let N1X = 0, N1Y = 0, N2X = 0, N2Y = 0;

  /* Ring / node state */
  let r1Op = 1, r1Th = 3, r1Pulse = 0;
  let n2Vis = false, n2Fade = 0, r2Op = 0.5, r2Th = 1.5, r2Pulse = 0;
  let flashA = 0, flashR = 50;

  function recomputeLayout() {
    RING_R = Math.min(50, W * 0.09);
    N1X = W * 0.44;
    N1Y = H * 0.5;
    N2X = N1X + RING_R * 2.8;
    N2Y = H * 0.5;
  }

  /* ── Particles (max 20) ── */
  interface Pt {
    x: number; y: number; vx: number; vy: number;
    alpha: number; active: boolean; resolved: boolean;
    breached: boolean; breachFlash: number;
    target: number; wobOff: number;
  }
  const pts: Pt[] = [];
  let nextSpawn = 0;

  function mkPt(): Pt {
    return { x: 0, y: 0, vx: 0, vy: 0, alpha: 0, active: false,
             resolved: false, breached: false, breachFlash: 0,
             target: 0, wobOff: 0 };
  }

  function spawnAt(tgt: number, dist: number) {
    let p = pts.find(q => !q.active);
    if (!p) {
      if (pts.length >= 20) return;
      p = mkPt(); pts.push(p);
    }
    const tx = tgt === 0 ? N1X : N2X;
    const ty = tgt === 0 ? N1Y : N2Y;
    const angle = Math.random() * Math.PI * 2;
    p.x = tx + Math.cos(angle) * dist;
    p.y = ty + Math.sin(angle) * dist;
    const dx = tx - p.x, dy = ty - p.y;
    const d = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy) || 1;
    const spd = 0.4 + Math.random() * 0.15;
    p.vx = (dx / d) * spd; p.vy = (dy / d) * spd;
    p.alpha = 0; p.active = true; p.resolved = false;
    p.breached = false; p.breachFlash = 0;
    p.target = tgt; p.wobOff = Math.random() * Math.PI * 2;
  }

  function spawn(tgt: number) {
    spawnAt(tgt, RING_R + 70 + Math.random() * 90);
  }

  function resetState() {
    frame = 0; globalFade = 1; nextSpawn = 15;
    r1Op = 1; r1Th = 3; r1Pulse = 0;
    n2Vis = false; n2Fade = 0; r2Op = 0.5; r2Th = 1.5; r2Pulse = 0;
    flashA = 0; flashR = RING_R;
    pts.forEach(p => { p.active = false; });
    /* Pre-seed 3 particles already approaching ring 1 */
    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
      spawnAt(0, RING_R + 18 + Math.random() * 30);
      const p = pts[pts.length - 1];
      if (p) p.alpha = 0.065;
    }
  }

  /* ── Update ── */
  function update() {
    /* ---- Phase state ---- */
    if (frame < P_CALM) {
      r1Op = 1; r1Th = 3;
    } else if (frame < P_DEGRADE) {
      const t = (frame - P_CALM) / (P_DEGRADE - P_CALM);
      r1Op = 1 - t * 0.88;
      r1Th = 3 - t * 2.5;
    } else if (frame < P_EXPOSED) {
      r1Op = 0.08; r1Th = 0.4;
    } else if (frame < P_FLASH) {
      /* Snap restoration in ~12 frames */
      const t = Math.min(1, (frame - P_EXPOSED) / 12);
      r1Op = 0.08 + t * 0.92;
      r1Th = 0.4 + t * 2.6;
      if (frame === P_EXPOSED + 1) {
        r1Pulse = 1; flashA = 0.9; flashR = RING_R;
        for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) spawnAt(0, RING_R + 10 + Math.random() * 22);
      }
    } else if (frame < P_APPEAR) {
      r1Op = 1; r1Th = 3;
      const t = (frame - P_FLASH) / (P_APPEAR - P_FLASH);
      n2Vis = true; n2Fade = t;
      r2Op = 0.5; r2Th = 1.5;
    } else if (frame < P_DUAL) {
      r1Op = 1; r1Th = 3; n2Fade = 1;
      const t = (frame - P_APPEAR) / (P_DUAL - P_APPEAR);
      r2Op = 0.5 - t * 0.42;
      r2Th = 1.5 - t * 1.1;
    } else if (frame < P_HOLD) {
      r2Op = 0.08; r2Th = 0.4;
    } else {
      globalFade = Math.max(0, 1 - (frame - P_HOLD) / (CYCLE - P_HOLD));
    }

    /* Pulse + flash decay */
    r1Pulse = Math.max(0, r1Pulse - 0.022);
    r2Pulse = Math.max(0, r2Pulse - 0.022);
    if (flashA > 0) { flashA = Math.max(0, flashA - 0.025); flashR += 1.8; }

    /* ---- Spawn particles ---- */
    if (frame >= nextSpawn) {
      if (frame < P_APPEAR) {
        /* Phases 1-5: target node 1 only */
        spawn(0);
        nextSpawn = frame + 24 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 14);
      } else if (frame < P_DUAL) {
        /* Phase 6: target both; late spawns close for hold visibility */
        const late = (frame - P_APPEAR) / (P_DUAL - P_APPEAR);
        if (late > 0.65) {
          spawnAt(Math.random() < 0.5 ? 0 : 1, RING_R + 14 + Math.random() * 22);
        } else {
          spawn(Math.random() < 0.5 ? 0 : 1);
        }
        nextSpawn = frame + 20 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 12);
      }
    }

    /* ---- Move + resolve particles ---- */
    pts.forEach(p => {
      if (!p.active) return;

      /* Fade in */
      if (p.alpha < 0.065) p.alpha = Math.min(0.065, p.alpha + 0.004);

      /* Perpendicular wobble */
      const pLen = Math.sqrt(p.vx * p.vx + p.vy * p.vy);
      let wobX = 0, wobY = 0;
      if (pLen > 0.0001) {
        const w = Math.sin(frame * 0.03 + p.wobOff) * 0.04;
        wobX = (-p.vy / pLen) * w;
        wobY = (p.vx / pLen) * w;
      }
      p.x += p.vx + wobX;
      p.y += p.vy + wobY;

      /* Breach flash decay */
      if (p.breachFlash > 0) p.breachFlash = Math.max(0, p.breachFlash - 0.022);

      /* Ring collision */
      if (!p.resolved) {
        const nx = p.target === 0 ? N1X : N2X;
        const ny = p.target === 0 ? N1Y : N2Y;
        const rOp = p.target === 0 ? r1Op : (n2Vis ? r2Op : 1);
        const dx = p.x - nx, dy = p.y - ny;
        const dist = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);

        if (dist < RING_R + 2) {
          p.resolved = true;
          if (Math.random() < 1 - rOp) {
            /* Breach: particle slips through */
            p.breached = true;
            p.breachFlash = 1;
            if (p.target === 0) r1Pulse = Math.max(r1Pulse, 0.3);
            else r2Pulse = Math.max(r2Pulse, 0.3);
          } else {
            /* Bounce: reflect outward, slow down */
            if (dist > 0.01) {
              const nnx = dx / dist, nny = dy / dist;
              const dot = p.vx * nnx + p.vy * nny;
              p.vx = (p.vx - 2 * dot * nnx) * 0.25;
              p.vy = (p.vy - 2 * dot * nny) * 0.25;
              p.x = nx + nnx * (RING_R + 4);
              p.y = ny + nny * (RING_R + 4);
            }
          }
        }
      }

      /* Breached -> absorbed at center */
      if (p.breached) {
        const nx = p.target === 0 ? N1X : N2X;
        const ny = p.target === 0 ? N1Y : N2Y;
        const dx = p.x - nx, dy = p.y - ny;
        if (Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy) < 7) {
          if (p.target === 0) r1Pulse = Math.max(r1Pulse, 0.2);
          else r2Pulse = Math.max(r2Pulse, 0.2);
          p.active = false;
        }
      }

      /* Bounced particles fade out */
      if (p.resolved && !p.breached) {
        p.alpha -= 0.0025;
        if (p.alpha <= 0) p.active = false;
      }

      /* Cull off-screen */
      if (p.x < -40 || p.x > W + 40 || p.y < -40 || p.y > H + 40) p.active = false;
    });
  }

  /* ── Draw ── */
  function draw() {
    ctx!.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    ctx!.fillStyle = bgColor;
    ctx!.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);

    const a = globalFade;

    function drawNode(nx: number, ny: number, rOp: number, rTh: number,
                      nAlpha: number, pulse: number) {
      const ra = rOp * a;
      const na = nAlpha * a;

      /* Ring stroke */
      if (ra > 0.003) {
        ctx!.beginPath();
        ctx!.arc(nx, ny, RING_R, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.strokeStyle = storyA(ra);
        ctx!.lineWidth = rTh;
        ctx!.stroke();
      }

      /* Ring glow */
      if (ra > 0.06) {
        const rg = ctx!.createRadialGradient(
          nx, ny, Math.max(0, RING_R - 8), nx, ny, RING_R + 12);
        rg.addColorStop(0, storyA(0));
        rg.addColorStop(0.35, storyA(ra * 0.1));
        rg.addColorStop(0.65, storyA(ra * 0.1));
        rg.addColorStop(1, storyA(0));
        ctx!.beginPath();
        ctx!.arc(nx, ny, RING_R + 12, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = rg;
        ctx!.fill();
      }

      /* Central child node */
      if (na > 0.003) {
        ctx!.beginPath();
        ctx!.arc(nx, ny, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(na);
        ctx!.fill();
        const ng = ctx!.createRadialGradient(nx, ny, 0, nx, ny, 10);
        ng.addColorStop(0, dimA(na * 0.35));
        ng.addColorStop(1, dimA(0));
        ctx!.beginPath();
        ctx!.arc(nx, ny, 10, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = ng;
        ctx!.fill();
      }

      /* Impact / restoration pulse */
      if (pulse > 0.005) {
        const pa = pulse * a;
        const pr = RING_R + (1 - pulse) * 22;
        const pg = ctx!.createRadialGradient(nx, ny, 0, nx, ny, pr);
        pg.addColorStop(0, storyA(pa * 0.4));
        pg.addColorStop(0.5, storyA(pa * 0.15));
        pg.addColorStop(1, storyA(0));
        ctx!.beginPath();
        ctx!.arc(nx, ny, pr, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = pg;
        ctx!.fill();
      }
    }

    /* Node 1 (always visible) */
    drawNode(N1X, N1Y, r1Op, r1Th, 0.3, r1Pulse);

    /* Node 2 (conditional) */
    if (n2Vis) drawNode(N2X, N2Y, r2Op, r2Th, 0.3 * n2Fade, r2Pulse);

    /* Restoration flash expanding ring */
    if (flashA > 0.005) {
      const fa = flashA * a;
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(N1X, N1Y, flashR, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.strokeStyle = storyA(fa * 0.5);
      ctx!.lineWidth = 1.5;
      ctx!.stroke();
    }

    /* Particles */
    pts.forEach(p => {
      if (!p.active) return;
      const pa = p.alpha * a;
      if (pa < 0.002) return;

      /* Red breach flash glow */
      if (p.breachFlash > 0.008) {
        const fa = p.breachFlash * a;
        ctx!.beginPath();
        ctx!.arc(p.x, p.y, 3, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = redA(fa * 0.65);
        ctx!.fill();
        const fg = ctx!.createRadialGradient(p.x, p.y, 0, p.x, p.y, 9);
        fg.addColorStop(0, redA(fa * 0.3));
        fg.addColorStop(1, redA(0));
        ctx!.beginPath();
        ctx!.arc(p.x, p.y, 9, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = fg;
        ctx!.fill();
      }

      /* Particle dot */
      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(p.x, p.y, 2.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(pa);
      ctx!.fill();
    });
  }

  /* ── Static frame (reduced motion) ── */
  function drawStatic() {
    ctx!.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    ctx!.fillStyle = bgColor;
    ctx!.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);

    /* Node 1: bright ring (the fix holds) */
    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.arc(N1X, N1Y, RING_R, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.strokeStyle = storyA(0.85);
    ctx!.lineWidth = 3;
    ctx!.stroke();

    const rg1 = ctx!.createRadialGradient(
      N1X, N1Y, Math.max(0, RING_R - 6), N1X, N1Y, RING_R + 10);
    rg1.addColorStop(0, storyA(0));
    rg1.addColorStop(0.5, storyA(0.08));
    rg1.addColorStop(1, storyA(0));
    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.arc(N1X, N1Y, RING_R + 10, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.fillStyle = rg1;
    ctx!.fill();

    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.arc(N1X, N1Y, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(0.3);
    ctx!.fill();

    /* Node 2: faded ring (the next toy, already failing) */
    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.arc(N2X, N2Y, RING_R, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.strokeStyle = storyA(0.1);
    ctx!.lineWidth = 0.5;
    ctx!.stroke();

    ctx!.beginPath();
    ctx!.arc(N2X, N2Y, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(0.3);
    ctx!.fill();

    /* Static particles: bounced off ring 1, breached ring 2 */
    const sPts = [
      { a: -0.5, d: 1.35, t: 0 },
      { a:  0.9, d: 1.4,  t: 0 },
      { a:  2.3, d: 1.25, t: 0 },
      { a:  1.0, d: 0.4,  t: 1 },
      { a: -0.7, d: 0.35, t: 1 }
    ];
    sPts.forEach(s => {
      const nx = s.t === 0 ? N1X : N2X;
      const ny = s.t === 0 ? N1Y : N2Y;
      const px = nx + Math.cos(s.a) * RING_R * s.d;
      const py = ny + Math.sin(s.a) * RING_R * s.d;

      ctx!.beginPath();
      ctx!.arc(px, py, 2.5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx!.fillStyle = dimA(0.06);
      ctx!.fill();

      /* Red glow on breached particles inside ring 2 */
      if (s.t === 1 && s.d < 0.9) {
        const fg = ctx!.createRadialGradient(px, py, 0, px, py, 7);
        fg.addColorStop(0, redA(0.2));
        fg.addColorStop(1, redA(0));
        ctx!.beginPath();
        ctx!.arc(px, py, 7, 0, Math.PI * 2);
        ctx!.fillStyle = fg;
        ctx!.fill();
      }
    });
  }

  /* ── Loop ── */
  function tick() {
    frame++;
    if (frame >= CYCLE) resetState();
    update();
    draw();
    rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  }

  /* ── Resize ── */
  const ro = new ResizeObserver(() => {
    const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
    W = canvas!.offsetWidth; H = canvas!.offsetHeight;
    canvas!.width = W * dpr; canvas!.height = H * dpr;
    ctx!.scale(dpr, dpr);
    recomputeLayout();
    if (prefersReduced) drawStatic();
  });
  ro.observe(canvas);

  const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;
  W = canvas.offsetWidth; H = canvas.offsetHeight;
  canvas.width = W * dpr; canvas.height = H * dpr;
  ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);
  recomputeLayout();

  if (prefersReduced) {
    drawStatic();
    window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => { ro.disconnect(); });
  } else {
    resetState();
    const io = new IntersectionObserver(([e]) => {
      if (e.isIntersecting) { if (!rafId) rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick); }
      else { cancelAnimationFrame(rafId); rafId = 0; }
    }, { threshold: 0.01 });
    io.observe(canvas);
    window.addEventListener('pagehide', () => {
      cancelAnimationFrame(rafId); io.disconnect(); ro.disconnect();
    });
  }
})();
</script>
